3.9     2009-09-29

        Starting Aug 20, 2009 TAMDAR data can be identifed as DATASRC 4, 7 or 8, 
        whereas before it was only type 4.  Fixed the API to include all the 
        new types.

        Added the snow level variable to MAP's map_variable_list.txt document.

        FILES CHANGED:

        doc/INSTALL.unix
        doc/INSTALL.windows
        doc/map_variable_list.txt
        doc/README
        doc/RELEASE_NOTES
        src/muaptmoi.f


3.8     2009-09-09

        Added New England Pilot Project stations (NEPP), Historical Climate 
        Network Modernization (HCN), and Climate Reference Network (CRN) 
        surface providers.  Note that the NEPP network, and the Alabama 
        stations in the HCN networks, were formerly in the COOP network.  
        Archive access to the COOP network prior to this change will still 
        be available.  Many new variables have been added to these datasets 
        that were not available in the COOP dataset.  See the variable lists 
        in this directory for details.

        Added archive temperature and precipitation processing for CRN and 
        HCN data.  NCDC creates the "official" temperature and accumulated
        precipitation data a couple hours after real-time.  Both the values
        reported in real-time, and the official archive values are available.
        If the user asks for T or PCP1H, and the archive version is available,
        it will be returned, otherwise the real-time value will be returned.
        Users wishing to access the real-time and/or archive values directly
        can specifically request those variables (see sfc_*_variable_list.txt
        for details).

        * Note that the above dataset changes will only go into effect when
        the next MADIS processing version release is done, which is
        expected to be in the September-November 2009 timeframe.

        Added the TAMAIR character variable to ACARS dataset.  This is used
        to identify which TAMDAR airline provided the data for each observation.

        Added the following WISDOM variables:

        T         air temperature
        RH        relative humidity
        CUTDOWN   cutdown flag
        PCALC     pressure calculated from height

        The WISDOM pressure (P) variable is now measured instead of being 
        calculated.  The WISDOM circular error (CIRCERR) variable has been 
        removed.
        
        * Note that as of this writing, the P, T, and RH variables are expected 
        to be of poor quality, and the QC will flag them as "subjectively bad".

        Changed the instructions on how to link to the OPeNDAP/DODS-enabled
        netCDF library in the makefiles.

        Added additional code value for "ice is present" (ICECOND value 4) 
        for TAMDAR airlines.  Previously all icing present conditions were
        mislabled as Delta airlines (value 1).

        Added snow level (SNOWLEV) to MAP dataset.

        Added correct identification for NOAA-19 in the satellite soundings
        and radiances.  Previously it had been erroneously identified as
        NOAA-32.
 
        Fixed a bug with the CSV output option in hydrodump.f and sfcdump.f.
        Those programs were using the last variable asked for by the user to
        determine the number of records to output.  If the last variable
        didn't have as many records with non-missing data as did the variable
        with the most records, then too few records would have been output.

        Changed madis_ingest.f so that it no longer initializes all
        subsystems at the beginning of the program.  Any programs using the
        API library can no longer have multiple subsystems initialized at
        the same time.

        Fixed the distance formula calculation in m_rdisll.f.  With unusually
        large distances (i.e., 30 degrees of latitude or longitude) errors
        of up to 15% would occur with the old formula.

        Increased MXNPN_P to 160, MXHYDRO_P to 15000, and MXRDMTR_P to 1800.

        Increased MXSTA_P to 300000.

        Fixed filter options 1, 2, and 3 in WISDOM dataset.

        Increased the size of stations and observations field in the sfcdump 
        text output to 6 spaces.

        Linux binaries are not long OPeNDAP enabled.  Users will have to 
        compile source code to create their own OPeNDAP enabled binaries.
        This is the only way to ensure they are compatible on their system.

        Miscellaneous internal software cleanup changes.

