VERSION COMMENTS
------- --------
3.7     2008-07-25

        Added the High Frequency METAR data to the surface dataset, and 
        added the WISDOM balloon wind dataset.  Neither of these datasets
        is yet available, but will be added to MADIS later this year.

        Fixed a bug in the sfcdump CSV output. The fix removes the 
        feature which required atleast one mesonet provider site with 
        data in the output selection.

        Fixed bug that caused bad data for SOA's SKYCVLB.

        Separated each dataset's unique constants into their own include
        files.  Moved universal constants and commons to their own include
        files.  This changed the include files used in many subroutines that
        included MADISCON and/or MADISCOM.

        Subroutines that the include file changed from MADISCON to INTQC1CON1
         m_chckqc.f
         mchgtim.f
         m_clrqc.f
         m_cnvttm.f
         m_cvjlmd.f
         m_cvwftat.f
         m_eswinv.f
         m_gti4tm.f
         m_intht.f
         m_intp.f
         minttim.f
         m_loght.f
         m_mkfnam.f
         m_mki4tm.f
         m_mkwfnm.f
         m_phtint.f
         m_setqc.f
         m_xgrid.f
         m_ygrid.f
         m_ztopsa.f

        Subroutines that the include file changed from MADISCON to
        INTQC1CON2.
         mrddep.f
         mrdchr.f

        Subroutines that the include files changed from MADISCON and
        MADISCOM to INTQC1COM1 and INTQC1CON1.
         merror.f

        Subroutines that the include file changed from MADISCON to
        INTQC1CON1 and RAOBCON.
         m_ctrn2dim.f
         m_rtrn2dim.f

        Subroutines that the include files changed from MADISCON and
        MADISCOM to INTQC1COM1, INTQC1CON2, and RAOBCON.
         mrdraoblev.f

        Moved temporary storage origination up a level in several
        subroutines to allow more reuse of subroutines.  This affects
        several routines that included MADISTMP.  The effect is two-fold:
        changes which subroutines includes MADISTMP, and changes the 
        number of variables in the subroutine calls.  

        Subroutines that no longer include MADISTMP and MADISCON, but
        have an additional input argument.
         m_cswap.f
         m_dswap.f
         m_iswap.f
         m_lswap.f
         m_rswap.f

        Subroutines that added the include MADISTMP.
         mgtnum.f

        Reduced the size of MXDATA_P to 32500 from 35000.  This is
        still larger than any variable's hourly data needs.

        Reduced the memory footprint of the sfcdump.exe binary by
        reducing the size of the surface csv space to 560 
        characters from 650.  Also changed how the number of 
        variables allowed was calculated from a pre-defined number 
        of variables to length of output string.  This should keep 
        the count of number-data variables with the full QC output 
        option about the same as before, but also allow users to 
        increase the count of number-data variables when using the 
        only QC data descriptors option.  The limitation is the 
        number of variables allowed could be reduced from before  
        when using the large text-data variables.
        
