VERSION COMMENTS
------- --------
3.1     2006-02-14

        Changed the maximum number of RAOB total levels to 405, and the
        maximum number of significant wind levels to 200.  

        Changes in various raob routines were made in order to keep the 
        significant winds that have observed pressures in different netCDF 
        variables from those used for significant winds with observed 
        heights.  This change was needed to keep MADIS files compatible 
        with the LAPS analysis software package.
     
        Changed the maximum number of surface records to 200000 in sfcdump.f
        and madis_ingest.f to match the increase in capacity made in version
        3.0.

        Moved "get station" memory area to level 1, the same as "get data".  
        Subroutines called by top level "get station" routines are level 2 
        and so on.  This was to reduce the memory foot print for the hp. The 
        memory location for mraobint moved to level 3.

